{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>They are whole with us.</b> Meaning, there is no hatred in their heart over the deed, to suspect guile:" "And their saying <b>their daughters we will take for ourselves</b> etc. — they contrived to say this so that the men of their city would believe that there is no resentment in their heart, for they consider them greater and better than themselves: since they are willing that their daughters be taken for wives etc., and the daughters of the family of Shechem they themselves will need to give to them — and this matter would indicate that they consider them greater and better than themselves, and this is the reason why they were not particular about the matter."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:45:55.755890846Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}